#
# NPC Demo Setup Batch Command File
# 
# This creates a demonstration world with various NPCs
# Run with: @batchcommand world/npc_demo_setup.ev
#

# Create main demo areas if they don't exist
@dig NPC Testing Hub
#
@desc NPC Testing Hub = A central hub for testing various NPC behaviors. Multiple corridors lead to specialized testing areas. Signs point to different sections: "Scanner Security", "Whisper Chambers", "Faction Territory", and "Market Square".

# Create scanner bot area
@dig/tel Scanner Security Zone = north,n;south,s = NPC Testing Hub
#
@desc Scanner Security Zone = A high-tech security checkpoint with gleaming metal walls and surveillance equipment. Red laser grids sweep across the room periodically. A large warning sign reads: "SCANNING IN PROGRESS - ALL ACTIVITIES MONITORED"

# Spawn scanner bot
@tel Scanner Security Zone
@spawn SCANNER_BOT

# Create whisper chambers
@dig/tel Whisper Chambers = east,e;west,w = NPC Testing Hub  
#
@desc Whisper Chambers = A dimly lit chamber with sound-dampening panels on the walls. The air feels thick and muffled, absorbing all but the softest sounds. A small plaque reads: "Silence is golden, whispers are wisdom."

# Spawn whisper bot
@tel Whisper Chambers
@spawn WHISPER_BOT

# Create faction territories
@dig/tel Tech Consortium Checkpoint = northeast,ne;southwest,sw = NPC Testing Hub
#
@desc Tech Consortium Checkpoint = A fortified checkpoint adorned with the chrome and blue colors of the Tech Consortium. Holographic displays show security alerts and faction propaganda. The hum of advanced technology fills the air.

# Spawn tech guard
@tel Tech Consortium Checkpoint
@spawn FACTION_GUARD

# Create nature cult area
@dig/tel Nature Cult Grove = northwest,nw;southeast,se = NPC Testing Hub
#
@desc Nature Cult Grove = A small indoor grove where nature has reclaimed technology. Vines wrap around defunct machinery, and bioluminescent fungi provide soft lighting. The air smells of earth and growing things.

# Spawn nature guard
@tel Nature Cult Grove
@spawn NATURE_GUARD

# Create market square
@dig/tel Market Square = south,s;north,n = NPC Testing Hub
#
@desc Market Square = A bustling marketplace where traders from all factions come to barter. Makeshift stalls line the walls, displaying various goods. The sound of haggling and commerce fills the air.

# Spawn merchant
@tel Market Square
@spawn MERCHANT_NPC

# Create scavenger outpost  
@dig/tel Scavenger Outpost = west,w;east,e = Market Square
#
@desc Scavenger Outpost = A ramshackle outpost built from salvaged materials. Everything here has been repurposed at least twice. Lookouts keep watch from elevated positions cobbled together from old shipping containers.

# Spawn scavenger lookout
@tel Scavenger Outpost
@spawn SCAVENGER_LOOKOUT

# Add some interactive objects to the areas
@tel Scanner Security Zone
@spawn COMBAT_DUMMY
@desc combat dummy = A reinforced training dummy marked with Tech Consortium insignia. It's designed to withstand security testing procedures.

@tel Nature Cult Grove  
@spawn WORN_DUMMY
@desc worn-out dummy = An ancient training dummy wrapped in vines and moss. The nature cult uses it to practice their combat techniques.

@tel Market Square
@spawn BOTTOMLESS_PIT
@desc bottomless pit = A mysterious pit in the corner of the market. Local legend says it leads to the old tunnels beneath the city. Merchants warn customers to stay away.

# Create a respawn room for the demo
@tel NPC Testing Hub
@dig/tel Central Respawn Chamber = down,d;up,u
#
@desc Central Respawn Chamber = The main respawn chamber for this facility. Resurrection technology hums quietly in the walls. This is where you'll return if you meet an untimely end during testing.

# Return to hub
@tel NPC Testing Hub

# Final setup message
@echo
@echo |y============================================|n
@echo |yNPC Demo World Setup Complete!|n
@echo |y============================================|n
@echo
@echo The following NPCs have been created:
@echo - Scanner Bot (Scanner Security Zone)
@echo - Whispering Guide (Whisper Chambers)  
@echo - Tech Consortium Guard (Tech Consortium Checkpoint)
@echo - Nature Cult Guardian (Nature Cult Grove)
@echo - Traveling Merchant (Market Square)
@echo - Scavenger Lookout (Scavenger Outpost)
@echo
@echo Interactive objects have also been placed for testing.
@echo
@echo |wUseful commands:|n
@echo - whisper <npc> = <message> - Whisper to NPCs
@echo - setfaction <faction> - Change your faction allegiance
@echo - say <message> - Speak normally (some NPCs react differently)
@echo - look <npc> - Examine NPCs
@echo
@echo |gEnjoy testing the NPCs!|n
@echo